# netsurf: native Node.prototype.compareDocumentPosition (patch 508)
# Generated 2026-11-28
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 507)
#
# compareDocumentPosition was a JS stand-in on the element prototype built
# on contains(): it answered FOLLOWING (4) both ways for two nodes neither
# containing the other. jQuery's uniqueSort (Sizzle sortOrder) then took
# its "disconnected" branch on every comparison -- ownerDocument reads
# (each through the window's document accessor), contains() calls, -1 for
# every pair -- and returned results out of document order. On rte.ie: 7
# sorts of 3,600-4,179 nodes, 2.5 s of the load's 5.75-5.9 s main-thread
# time in the sim.
#
# It is a C function on Node.prototype now, answering libdom's tree-order
# compare (508-libdom-compare-document-position.patch). The realm's
# document object (not an element-class wrapper) is matched by identity; a
# non-object argument throws Chromium's TypeError; an object that is no
# node of this realm is answered as disconnected (37).
#
# rte.ie main thread 5.9 -> 3.45 s in the sim (sorts 2.57 s -> 0.14 s;
# comparator calls per sort 144k -> 38k, a consistent comparator).
# Gate: JS-cdp / CSS-cdp-ref (every answer row for row against the answers
# written in; 507 differs in 83 rows).
